## Setup

Install Python dependencies:

    pip install bleak fastapi uvicorn websockets sqlalchemy passlib[bcrypt] itsdangerous jinja2 python-multipart

## Running the project

The backend runs directly on the host (NOT in Docker) because the BLE sensor
requires direct access to the system Bluetooth stack — bleak cannot reach
Bluetooth from inside a container on Windows/macOS.

1. Start the backend on the host:

       cd backend
       python main.py

   Server starts at http://localhost:8000

2. In another terminal, start the database container + Cloudflare tunnel:

       docker-compose up --build

   This starts:
   - SQLite database container (volume-mounted at /app/data/users.db)
   - Cloudflare tunnel: game.sensorproject.org → localhost:8000

## Architecture

    Browser / Godot game
        ↕  WebSocket /ws
    backend/main.py   (FastAPI, runs on host)
        ↕  BLE via bleak (direct host Bluetooth)
    Cycling sensor (XOSS / compatible CSC device)

    Cloudflare tunnel → localhost:8000  (remote / mobile access)

## Games

- Fishing game:  http://localhost:8000/FishingGame
- Space game:    http://localhost:8000/SpaceFunk
- BLE control:   http://localhost:8000/ble
